      "automation": {
        "mode": "manual-only",
        "note": "Manual-only. X's API is pay-per-use with no free tier (docs.x.com pricing, read 2026-10-24): Post: Create costs $0.015 per request and Post: Create (with URL) $0.200, so even a link-free API post costs cash and the Group spends none (requirement group-work-continues-on-zero-cash-compute). Posting by hand in the web app costs nothing, so X runs as link-free native posts written by the engine as packets and posted by a person, with the brand site in the profile's website field. A post needs no canonical link to participate; the gate still requires the provenance line, which is the post's only URL. If X adds a free tier, change the mode to api-allowed-bot-disclosed: automated accounts must use the official API only, enable the Automated label and say in the bio that the account is a bot and who operates it. AI-generated replies need X approval; this account does not reply."
      },
      "aiDisclosure": {
        "required": true,
        "offered": false,
        "mechanism": "text-label",
        "apiField": null,
        "textLabel": "AI-generated media"
      },
      "limits": {
